        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi again! Thanks so much for your enthusiasm!\r\n\r\nI usually prefer writing them on my own because of a joy I am getting while creating new API and functionality. However, I am totally not opposed to the idea of someone else implementing whole module (it basically was the case with 'mini.jump'). \r\n\r\nThe 'mini.clue' in particular has a certain idea behind it. I use and love 'folke/which-key' but it has a design decision which I really don't like: it completely relies on making a bunch of extra keybindings. So I have the idea to try to implement it without them, just by tracking user keys with `vim.on_key()`. Really not sure if it will work, to be honest (that design decision might be a necessity). To write this, you'll need to know/discover at least about:\r\n- Key tracking in Neovim.\r\n- How keymappings are created and executed.\r\n- How to create and manage floating windows.\r\n- Quite a bit of Lua to efficiently manage tables.\r\n\r\nAll in all, I can't really recommend this as a first time contribution (especially in case of not very deep Lua knowledge).\r\n\r\nIf you really want to contribute, I might suggest one of the following (in increasing order of complexity):\r\n\r\n- Spreading a word about existence and usefulness of this plugin. Write blog post, make a video, etc. It is **really** appreciated.\r\n- What is [described in 'CONTRIBUTING.md'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md), i.e. fix typos, add support of 'mini.nvim' to some color scheme plugin of your choice, etc.\r\n- I plan to make wiki page dedicated to examples of 'mini.ai' custom textobjects. There are already great examples of textobjects for line, buffer, diagnostic, git chunk. There might be more creative ways for you to explore.\r\n- Some small but non-trivial utility function in 'mini.misc'. One of the ideas I plan to implement is something similar to [FooSoft/vim-argwrap](https://github.com/FooSoft/vim-argwrap) but in Lua and using this [idea of an \"argument\"](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/93e0f4b2e886813c65c94c5071f08cac6aacaed1/lua/mini/ai.lua#L642).\r\n- If you want to implement whole module, there is 'mini.root'. I plan to write it after the next planned 'mini.align' and explained general design idea in more detail [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/pull/88#issuecomment-1154832882). Shouldn't require a lot of Neovim-specific knowledge here). It will be a long process because there are usually a lot of small details that I want to get right.\r\n\r\nAny from the above contributions will be welcome.",
